  "limitations": [
    "ssh-add exit 2 = could not connect to an agent; exit 1 = agent reachable but no identities (a fallback to another agent would show 0 or 1). When the default pipe was present its server was reached only if the client fell back, and that run's stdout was not saved.",
    "Forward-slash and space/Unicode pipe-name forms and non-System32 ssh-add builds are recorded as observations, not pass criteria.",
    "[O] supplementary diagnostic (scratch script, not harness output; tests/evidence/artifacts/g03/native-win/supplementary/diag-pipename.json): with SSH_AUTH_SOCK, both Win32-OpenSSH ssh-add builds (9.5p2, 10.0p2) reach pipes whose names are ASCII or contain spaces (exit 0, key listed) but fail on any name containing a non-ASCII character (exit 2, \"No such file or directory\", zero connections at the fixture), in backslash and forward-slash forms. The same kind of name worked through ssh.exe IdentityAgent in P-W03. Cause not established [U].",
    "Git for Windows MSYS ssh-add (OpenSSH_10.3p1) cannot use Windows named pipes: backslash form \"Device or resource busy\" (it opened the pipe as a file: the fixture logged a connection with no request), forward-slash form \"No such file or directory\".",
    "Top-level status and verdict cover only the rows that ran; rows listed as blocked in observed_result.sub_probe_status stay blocked with their own blocked_on.",
    "Promoted by M00-T04-G03-native-windows from environment.raw_record; fields added at promotion: environment.task/host/fixture/harness_provenance/raw_record/supplementary_ps51_record, observed_result.sub_probe_status, and the limitations after the harness-written ones. The supplementary Windows PowerShell 5.1 run of the same harness gave the same status and criteria."
